nds important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le05ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Talking About Cities"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you talk about cities with a long history, you can talk about their  modern or historical areas."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Adjectives to Describe a City\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Places in a City\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"modern<br> ancient<br> large <br>small <br>interesting<br> boring <br>exciting <br>beautiful\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"residence<br> hospital<br> mosque <br>aqueduct<br> ruins<br> mint <br>bakery<br> palace\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Sultans used the palace as a residence for 400 years!  "}, {"type": "example", "content": " It remained the world's largest cathedral for centuries. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "There were mosques, a hospital, bakeries, and a mint. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "Romans "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "people from ancient Rome "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: In ancient times Romans lived in Constantinople."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le05ob06aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about Turkey."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "aqueduct"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a structure like a bridge to carry water across land "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: In Turkey, you can visit the ruins of an aqueduct."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le05ob06aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sultan"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " the name for a ruler in some Muslim countries "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I can meet a real sultan in the palace."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le05ob06aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "residence"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a place where someone lives "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The Topkapi Palace was as a residence for Sultans."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le05ob06aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mint"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a place to make coins or money "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I want to go to the mint and buy a new coin."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le05ob06aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "thousand "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "1000"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Four thousand people lived in the Topkapii Palace at one time."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le05ob06aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "unfortunately "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "badly or unluckily "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Unfortunately, the gems from the Palace were lost."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le05ob06aud07"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go online and find a video about Istanbul